{"mode":"training","language":"en","altTextLanguage":"","title":"","instruction":{"english":"","german":""},"allowInstructionLineBreaks":false,"readingText":{"instruction":{"german":"","english":""},"content":"","configs":[]},"sequences":[{"instruction":{"german":"<p>Read the grammar box. Then complete the sentences with the adverb form of the adjective in brackets.<\/p>","english":""},"configs":[{"correctAnswer":"well","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_0","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_6\/p79_ex3\/"},{"correctAnswer":"fast","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_1","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_6\/p79_ex3\/"},{"correctAnswer":"high","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_2","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_6\/p79_ex3\/"},{"correctAnswer":"loudly","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_3","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_6\/p79_ex3\/"},{"correctAnswer":"angrily","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_4","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_6\/p79_ex3\/"},{"correctAnswer":"hard","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_5","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_6\/p79_ex3\/"}],"staticConfigs":[],"parts":["<p><b>Grammar | Adverbs of manner<\/b><\/p><p>We use adverbs of manner to describe <b>how<\/b> something happens:<em>She can sing <\/em><b><em>beautifully<\/em><\/b><em>.<\/em><\/p><p>We form most adverbs of manner by adding <em>-ly<\/em> to the adjective:<em>bad \u2013 badly<\/em>;<em> careful \u2013 carefully<\/em><\/p><p><em><span class=\"ql-cursor\">\ufeff<\/span><\/em>Some adverbs of manner are irregular:<em>good \u2013 well<\/em>;<em> fast \u2013 fast<\/em><\/p><p><br><\/p><p><b>1<\/b> I can\u2019t swim very <gap id=\"gap_0\"><\/gap> (good).<\/p><p><b>2<\/b> He doesn\u2019t run very <gap id=\"gap_1\"><\/gap> (fast) but he can jump very <gap id=\"gap_2\"><\/gap> (high).<\/p><p><b>3<\/b> You don\u2019t have to talk <gap id=\"gap_3\"><\/gap> (loud) \u2013 I\u2019m standing next to you!<\/p><p><b>4<\/b> \u2018Why did you forget your homework again?\u2019 asked the teacher, <gap id=\"gap_4\"><\/gap> (angry).<\/p><p><b>5<\/b> She tried very <gap id=\"gap_5\"><\/gap> (hard), but she couldn\u2019t understand the lesson.<\/p>"],"globalTypesConfigs":[{"type":"gap","widthMode":"asLongestWord","longestAlternativeSolutions":false,"ignoreCaseSensitivity":false}],"staticText":{"text":"<p><br><\/p>","backgroundColor":"lightgray","isSet":false}}]}